import json
from pathlib import Path
D=Path(__file__).parent;f=json.loads((D/'findings.json').read_text())
s=['# Tanzania: library expansion feasibility, 15 November 2026','', '**Five observed institutions/networks; five selected, zero reserves; shortfall of five against the ten-target goal.** Four successes use Koha; Zanzibar Library Services Board uses a custom OPAC. Nineteen substantial priorities were assessed, with additional specialized routes considered. Search-index records and catalog homepages were never counted as successful queries.','', 'A policy-aware Koha integration is the clearest near-term route through SNAL, SUZA, MUST and DarTU. TLSB remains the largest public-network opportunity in this screen, but its public website links to an iNDLS login route and this research did not establish an anonymous physical-book search. The [15 October 2026 TLSB update](https://www.tlsb.go.tz/news/tlsb-board-chairperson-commends-management-on-indls-development-directs-expansion-of-services-to-all-43-libraries-nationwide) states that iNDLS is used in **11 libraries**, with expansion to all **43** directed. This is not proof of 43 searchable collections.','', '## Marketplace, software and access','', 'Mainland public/national provision is organized through TLSB; Zanzibar has its own public library board. University libraries include large public and private institutions and specialized teaching/research networks. Their membership rules differ: DarTU advertises external membership at TZS 10,000/month; ZLSB advertises free standard membership for Zanzibaris, three books for fourteen days. Anonymous OPAC access does not establish a visitor’s borrowing eligibility. See the saved [DarTU service page](evidence/dartu-size.html) and [ZLSB service page](evidence/zanzibar-size.html).','', '[COTUL, described by EIFL](https://www.eifl.info/country/tanzania), is a high-leverage coordination, licensing and training network covering academic, research and special libraries. EIFL lists 96 members and separately says 47 institutions in its work; those are distinct scopes. No shared national physical-book union catalog was verified. Licensed electronic journals, ebook databases and institutional repositories must remain separate from local copy holdings.','', 'Koha is well evidenced by the four working deployments, Ardhi’s official library description, and a [2019 UDSM dissertation](https://libraryrepository.udsm.ac.tz/bitstreams/07f1b039-2656-4b06-9530-359ce03d9539/download) that purposively examined OUT, IFM and CBE as Koha adopters. This supports adoption, not a national market-share percentage. Historical ABCD reports for Sokoine/Mzumbe do not override current Koha pages. Makumira identifies Mandarin Oasis and its endpoint identifies Mandarin 5.7.11; its live page displayed “Startup failed.” ZLSB’s custom template does not establish a named backend LMS.','', '## Major priorities','', 'These are priorities, **not a size ranking**. Counts have different dates and units, and some are explicit institutional proxies. Large inaccessible libraries remain visible.','', '| Institution/network | Source-backed scale or proxy | Observed outcome |','|---|---|---|']
for p in f['major_library_priorities']:
 s.append('| '+p['name']+' | ['+p['size_claim'].replace('|','/')+']('+p['source_url']+') | '+p['outcome']+' |')
s+=['','## Actual title queries','', 'All five queries below returned HTTP 200. Exact submitted URLs, final URLs, timestamps and records are in [findings.json](findings.json); each raw response has a paired request metadata file. Queries that returned a single record could redirect directly to its detail page.','', '| Selected institution | Exact query | Returned book / identity | Observed holdings |','|---|---|---|---|']
for l in f['libraries']:
 b=l['books'][0];s.append('| '+l['name']+' | ['+l['query']['text']+']('+l['query']['url']+') | '+b['title']+' — '+b['author']+'; ID '+str(b['record_id'])+' | '+b['holdings']+' |')
s+=['','## Request evidence and integration implications','']
for l in f['libraries']:
 q=l['query'];s+=['### '+l['name'],'',f"`{q['method']} {q['url']}`",'',f"Checked `{q['checked_at_utc']}`; HTTP{q['http_status']}; final URL `{q['effective_url']}`. {q['count_note']}",'',f"Evidence: [query response]({q['evidence_path']}), [request metadata]({q['metadata_path']}), [robots metadata]({l['robots']['evidence_path']}). {l['reader_access']}",'']
 if l['platform']['family']=='Custom ZLSB OPAC':
  s+=['The result area says **Showing 5 titles for Uchu** and contains exact-title *Uchu*, while New Arrivals remains elsewhere on the same page. The custom parser must isolate query cards and their embedded detail modals. Modal ID19 is observed, but no standalone record URL was demonstrated. “In Collection” is the strongest justified status; no branch/copy circulation is exposed. The advertised 50,000+ titles conflicts with the OPAC header’s 2,002+. Five branches establish the network proxy, not catalog completeness.','']
 else:
  s+=['Existing Koha adapter reuse is a candidate, not tested compatibility. Handle single-result redirects, retain edition/biblionumber identity, preserve reference/special-reserve restrictions, and check template-specific holding labels.','']
 if l['integration']['blockers']:s+=[' '.join(l['integration']['blockers']),'']
s+=['## Blocked and unverified alternatives','', '| Candidate/route | Blocker | Evidence |','|---|---|---|']
for b in f['blocked_or_unverified']:s.append('| ['+b['name']+']('+b['url']+') | '+b['reason']+' | [metadata]('+b['evidence_path']+') |')
s+=['', 'UDSM’s robots policy explicitly excludes `/cgi-bin/koha/opac-search.pl` and specifies a 20-second crawl delay; no search was sent. A separately allowed collection-summary page timed out. MUHAS’s main website additionally served an Access Verification page; that was not treated as an ordinary HTML fallback. Other robots503/timeouts/400 remained unresolved and were not followed by catalog searches.','', 'Makumira’s website robots URL returned an ordinary university homepage fallback, manually inspected with no challenge or exclusion. One public library-page read was used to discover its explicit public-IP Mandarin link. That origin’s robots returned404; its catalog startup then failed. No internal/private IP link, credential, challenge bypass or TLS bypass was used. SJUT’s public page bundles were inspected only to follow the displayed LIMS link; the separately linked catalog’s robots503 stopped further checks.','', '## Limits and reproducibility','']
for x in f['limitations']:s.append('- '+x)
s+=['','The shared `../probe.py` performed bounded GET requests under the transparent MyBookshelfResearch user agent, normal TLS validation, at most three independent origins concurrently. Each catalog was checked against robots first. A404 means no published rules were observed, not affirmative reuse permission. No contact, authentication, account creation, hold, reservation or product change occurred.','', 'Saved responses are bounded; anonymous form tokens and the failed Mandarin session identifier were redacted after collection. Metadata retains the original response hash and a separate sanitized artifact hash where redaction occurred. Cookies were never persisted. Reproduction starts from the official public form rather than reusing a captured session or nonce. Source discovery exports are retained as contextual evidence; they are not successful catalog responses.','']
(D/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(s))
